From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:16:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/hevc: say in a debug line how many slices waited for
 setup to end

One line at AV_LOG_DEBUG for each access unit whose slices the decoder
set aside until ff_thread_finish_setup() (multilayer frame threading),
with their number, so that a test can tell where that path was taken and
where it was not.
---
 libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
index 3e3afa5..b67e64b 100644
--- a/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/hevc/hevcdec.c
@@ -3842,6 +3842,8 @@ static int decode_deferred_slices(HEVCContext *s)
             ret = err;
         }
     }
+    av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG,
+           "Decoded %u slice(s) set aside until setup had ended.\n", s->nb_deferred);
     s->nb_deferred = 0;
 
     return ret;
-- 
2.53.0

